<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Crisóstomo Falcón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1820–1870</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Crisóstomo Falcón was a Venezuelan general and Liberal leader who commanded the federalist forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-war">Federal War</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezequiel-zamora">Ezequiel Zamora</a> in 1860. Following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche">Treaty of Coche</a> in 1863 he became president, and the constitution of 1864 renamed the country the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Venezuela. Weakened by regional revolts, his government fell to the Blue Revolution in 1868.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-crisostomo-falcon.jpg" alt="Juan Crisóstomo Falcón" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martín Tovar y Tovar (1827 - 1902) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martin_Tovar_y_Tovar_23.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
